/api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally on Firefox 155 on Linux, I got this error on the first try when clicking **Start Godot editor**:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1320\" height=\"525\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dbb6f1f4-a409-4e0b-99c2-5304e318dc64\" />\r\n\r\nHowever, on the second try (and on the first try in Chromium 152), it works fine:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1320\" height=\"234\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa987a84-b2fa-4d17-9cc3-a71036f41b8b\" />\r\n\r\nThere are still some warnings about character encoding that could be addressed.\r\n\r\nI'm using `platform/web/serve.py -r $PWD/bin/.web_zip/` to test this. I unregistered the previous service worker to make sure I'm up-to-date. This issue consistently occurred in a given browser tab, so I assume it was some other kind of caching issue.\r\n\r\nCode looks good to me.\r\n\r\n___\r\n\r\nAs an aside, I noticed that relying on <kbd>F5</kbd> autosaving scenes before running the project doesn't work in the web editor (possibly because the project starts before scenes are done saving). When running the project, it'll display the state of the scene *before* it was saved. This issue only occurs in Firefox, not Chromium.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123485#pullrequestreview-5281197682","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123485","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123485#pullrequestreview-5281197682"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123485"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-22T17:03:42Z","commit_id":"8562644777a7b01833ff5e5a34d39d9878975271"},{"id":5334954435,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPfzxww","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://a